;; The module _locale (PY6c; Modules/_localemodule.c) over musl's locale model, the C library of the target
;; (Alpine): setlocale accepts any name of at most 23 bytes without '/' (another name is C.UTF-8's), "POSIX" is
;; "C", C.UTF-8 is "C" beyond LC_CTYPE, LC_ALL's query names every category when they differ ("A;B;C;D;E;F");
;; LC_CTYPE starts from the environment (LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, LANG, else C.UTF-8) as CPython's startup sets it, the
;; others from "C". musl has no numeric, monetary, time or message data: localeconv and nl_langinfo are the C
;; locale's in every locale but CODESET (ASCII in C, else UTF-8), strcoll is wcscmp and strxfrm the identity,
;; gettext returns its message. CHAR_MAX is the C char's (unsigned on arm64).

